  "prompt": "You are an expert frontend developer and UI designer. Create a single-page, standalone HTML document containing a complex, animated \"System Monitor\" dashboard with a heavy Cyberpunk / Sci-Fi aesthetic.\n\nSTRICT TECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS:\n1. ALL HTML, CSS, and JavaScript must be contained within a single file. Do not import external libraries (no React, no Tailwind, no external CSS). You may use Google Fonts (e.g., 'Share Tech Mono' or 'Orbitron').\n2. Do NOT output markdown code blocks (```html). Start exactly with <!DOCTYPE html> and end with </html>.\n\nLAYOUT SPECIFICATIONS:\n1. The layout must feature a permanent, fixed sidebar on the left side (approx 250px wide) containing a futuristic user profile and at least four functional-looking navigation buttons.\n2. The main content area must utilize a responsive CSS Grid structure to display at least three distinct data panels.\n\nAESTHETIC & GEOMETRIC SPECIFICATIONS:\n1. The color palette must be dark mode: deep black backgrounds (#050505), with neon cyan, hot magenta, and toxic green accents.\n2. To achieve a seamless Sci-Fi look, the primary data panels must feature an inward-curving top corner (a custom border-radius or clip-path cut-out), giving it a highly structured, non-boxy appearance.\n3. Include a subtle, semi-transparent CSS \"scanline\" overlay across the entire viewport to simulate a CRT monitor.\n\nANIMATION & INTERACTIVITY SPECIFICATIONS (JavaScript required):\n1. Glitch Effect: The main dashboard header text must feature a CSS keyframe animation that occasionally \"glitches\" (splitting colors or offsetting text for a split second).\n2. Live Telemetry: One of the grid panels must contain a \"CPU/RAM Load\" bar chart or circular progress indicator. Use JavaScript to randomly update these values and animate the bars/circles every 800 milliseconds.\n3. Terminal Output: Another panel must act as a terminal window. Use JavaScript to automatically append simulated, matrix-style data logs (e.g., \"0x00FF... BYPASSING SECURITY...\") that scroll continuously.\n\nEnsure the final output is visually stunning, responsive, and immediately interactive upon loading.\n",
  "rawOutput": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<title>Cyberpunk System Monitor</title>\n<link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com\">\n<link href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/otf/Share_Tech_Mono/Regular?font=italic&display=swap\" rel=\"stylesheet\">\n<style>\n/* Base styles */\nbody {\n    margin: 0;\n    background: #050505;\n    color: #e0e0e0;\n    font-family: 'Share Tech Mono', monospace;\n    overflow-x: hidden;\n}\n/* Scanline overlay */\n.scanline {\n    position: fixed;\n    top: 0;\n    left: 0;\n    width: 100vw;\n    height: 100vh;\n    background: rgba(255,255,255,0.02);\n    pointer-events: none;\n    z-index: -1;\n}\n/* Header */\nheader {\n    height: 60px;\n    background: #010100;\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    justify-content: center;\n    padding: 0 15px;\n    border-radius: 20px 0 0 20px;\n    box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);\n}\nheader .glitch-text {\n    font-size: 1.2rem;\n    animation: glitch 0.5s infinite alternate;\n}\n@keyframes glitch {\n    0%, 100% {color: #00FFFF;}\n    50% {color: #FF0000;}\n}\n.header-title {\n    font-weight: bold;\n    text-shadow: 0 2px 4px rgba(0,0,0,0.3);\n}\n/* Sidebar */\n.sidebar {\n    position: fixed;\n    left: 0;\n    top: 0;\n    width: 250px;\n    background: #030a15;\n    color: #a0a0c0;\n    height: 100vh;\n    display: flex;\n    flex-direction: column;\n    padding: 15px;\n    box-sizing: border-box;\n    overflow-y: hidden;\n}\n.sidebar nav {\n    background: #080a0e;\n    border: none;\n    padding: 10px;\n    cursor: pointer;\n    flex: 1;\n}\n.sidebar nav button {\n    width: 100%;\n    padding: 10px;\n    border: none;\n    background: transparent;\n    color: #ff00ff;\n    font-size: 1rem;\n    cursor: pointer;\n    border-radius: 5px;\n}\n/* Main content grid */\n.main-grid {\n    display: grid;\n    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(300px, 1fr));\n    gap: 20px;\n    padding: 20px;\n}\n.panel {\n    background: #040a12;\n    border-radius: 15px 8px 8px 15px;\n    padding: 20px;\n    box-shadow: 0 4px 15px rgba(0,0,0,0.4);\n}\n.panel1 {grid-column: span 2;}\n.panel2 {grid-column: span 1;}\n.panel3 {grid-column: span 1;}\n/* Terminal panel */\n#terminal {\n    background: #0a0a1a;\n    color: #00ffcc;\n    padding: 10px;\n    white-space: pre;\n    font-family: 'Share Tech Mono', monospace;\n    height: 300px;\n    overflow-y: auto;\n}\n#terminal::-webkit-scrollbar {display: none;}\n/* Responsive adjustments */\n@media (max-width: 800px) {\n    .sidebar {flex-direction: column;}\n}\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div class=\"scanline\"></div>\n<div class=\"sidebar\">\n    <button class=\"glitch-text\">System Monitor</button>\n    <button>Dashboard</button>\n    <button>Analytics</button>\n    <button>Security</button>\n    <button>Logs</button>\n</div>\n<header>\n    <div class=\"glitch-text\">System Monitor</div>\n</header>\n<main class=\"main-grid\">\n    <div class=\"panel\">\n        <h2>CPU Metrics</h2>\n        <p>Load: <span id=\"cpuVal\">0%</span> / Memory: <span id=\"memVal\">0%</span></p>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"panel\">\n        <h2>Network Status</h2>\n        <p>Ping: 12ms / Jitter: 3ms</p>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"panel\">\n        <h2>System Clock</h2>\n        <p id=\"time\">00:00:00</p>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"panel terminal-panel\">\n        <h2>Terminal</h2>\n        <pre id=\"log\">0x00FF... BYPASSING SECURITY...</pre>\n    </div>\n</main>\n<script>\n// Glitch effect toggle\nfunction toggleGlitch() {\n    document.querySelector('.glitch-text').classList.toggle('active');\n}\nsetInterval(toggleGlitch, 1500);\n// CPU/RAM load update\nfunction updateMetrics() {\n    const cpu = (Math.random() * 100).toFixed(0) + '%';\n    const mem = (Math.random() * 100).toFixed(0) + '%';\n    document.getElementById('cpuVal').textContent = cpu;\n    document.getElementById('memVal').textContent = mem;\n    // circular progress animation\n    const canvas = document.createElement('canvas');\n    canvas.width = 200;\n    canvas.height = 200;\n    document.body.appendChild(canvas);\n    const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');\n    ctx.fillStyle = '#00FFFF';\n    const radius = Math.min(100, Math.random() * 150);\n    ctx.beginPath();\n    ctx.arc(radius, radius, radius, 0, Math.PI * 2 * (Math.random() * 0.5 + 0.5));\n    ctx.fill();\n}\nsetInterval(updateMetrics, 800);\n// Simulate matrix logs\nconst logLines = [\n    \"0x00FF... BYPASSING SECURITY...\",\n    \"ACCESS GRANTED: CORE_IDENTITY_VERIFIED\",\n    \"ERROR: NEUROMANCER DETECTED\",\n    \"SYSTEM BOOTING...\",\n    \"WARNING: MALWARE SIGNATURE DETECTED\",\n    \"INFO: BACKUP SYNC COMPLETE\"\n];\nlet lineIndex = 0;\nfunction scrollLogs() {\n    const el = document.getElementById('log');\n    el.scrollTop = el.scrollHeight;\n    setTimeout(() => scrollLogs(), 100);\n}\nsetInterval(scrollLogs, 100);\n</script>\n</body>\n</html>",
